RACE_INFO_DRACTHYR_H = "Created by Neltharion the Earth-Warder, the essence of dragons was combined with the adaptability of mortal races to create an elite armed force able to shift between draconic and humanoid form. Long held in magical stasis, this army awakens to face a new threat on the Dragon Isles. It is in the Forbidden Reach that the adventure begins for dracthyr who wish to recover their memories before confronting a new reality.";
RACE_INFO_DRACTHYR_H_FEMALE = "Created by Neltharion the Earth-Warder, the essence of dragons was combined with the adaptability of mortal races to create an elite armed force able to shift between draconic and humanoid form. Long held in magical stasis, this army awakens to face a new threat on the Dragon Isles. It is in the Forbidden Reach that the adventure begins for dracthyr who wish to recover their memories before confronting a new reality.";
RACE_INFO_VULPERA_A = "Long ago, a faction of zealous gnomes set out to improve their bodies and minds. Settled on the isolated island of Mechagon, they conducted experiments using ancient technology to rid themselves of the 'curse of flesh' and become true living machines. After confronting the excesses of mechanization at any cost, they eventually found the ideal balance between flesh and steel. Now reunited with their gnome cousins, the Mechagnomes put their tenacity and ingenuity to the service of the Alliance.";
RACE_INFO_VULPERA_A_FEMALE = "Long ago, a faction of zealous gnomes set out to improve their bodies and minds. Settled on the isolated island of Mechagon, they conducted experiments using ancient technology to rid themselves of the 'curse of flesh' and become true living machines. After confronting the excesses of mechanization at any cost, they eventually found the ideal balance between flesh and steel. Now reunited with their gnome cousins, the Mechagnomes put their tenacity and ingenuity to the service of the Alliance.";
RACE_INFO_HIGHMOUNTAINTAUREN = "Despite their small stature, the gnomes of Khaz Modan have put their great intelligence to use to secure their place in history. Indeed, their underground kingdom, Gnomeregan, was once a steam-powered technological marvel. Sadly, the city was lost following a massive trogg invasion. Its builders are now wanderers roaming dwarven lands, helping their allies however they can.";
RACE_INFO_HIGHMOUNTAINTAUREN_FEMALE = "Despite their small stature, the gnomes of Khaz Modan have put their great intelligence to use to secure their place in history. Indeed, their underground kingdom, Gnomeregan, was once a steam-powered technological marvel. Sadly, the city was lost following a massive trogg invasion. Its builders are now wanderers roaming dwarven lands, helping their allies however they can.";
RACE_INFO_HIGHELF = "The tauren tirelessly strive to preserve the balance of nature and fulfill the will of their goddess, the Earth Mother. Recently attacked by centaurs, the tauren would have been wiped out had they not chanced upon the orcs, who helped them repel their enemies. To honor this blood debt, the tauren joined the Horde, strengthening the bond of friendship between the two races.";
RACE_INFO_HIGHELF_FEMALE = "The tauren tirelessly strive to preserve the balance of nature and fulfill the will of their goddess, the Earth Mother. Recently attacked by centaurs, the tauren would have been wiped out had they not chanced upon the orcs, who helped them repel their enemies. To honor this blood debt, the tauren joined the Horde, strengthening the bond of friendship between the two races.";
RACE_INFO_DARKIRONDWARF_H = "Known for their fiery temperament and unshakeable resolve, the Dark Iron dwarves have long been at odds with the other clans: a failed coup in Ironforge sparked the War of the Three Hammers, and many Dark Irons fought in the name of Ragnaros, the Firelord. Although part of the clan has sworn allegiance to Regent Queen Moira Thaurissan, the rest refuse to rejoin their kin. Yet the Alliance needs a united Dark Iron clan to harness the power of Azerite in its war against the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_DARKIRONDWARF_H_FEMALE = "Known for their fiery temperament and unshakeable resolve, the Dark Iron dwarves have long been at odds with the other clans: a failed coup in Ironforge sparked the War of the Three Hammers, and many Dark Irons fought in the name of Ragnaros, the Firelord. Although part of the clan has sworn allegiance to Regent Queen Moira Thaurissan, the rest refuse to rejoin their kin. Yet the Alliance needs a united Dark Iron clan to harness the power of Azerite in its war against the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_DARKIRONDWARF = "Known for their fiery temperament and unshakeable resolve, the Dark Iron dwarves have long been at odds with the other clans: a failed coup in Ironforge sparked the War of the Three Hammers, and many Dark Irons fought in the name of Ragnaros, the Firelord. Although part of the clan has sworn allegiance to Regent Queen Moira Thaurissan, the rest refuse to rejoin their kin. Yet the Alliance needs a united Dark Iron clan to harness the power of Azerite in its war against the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_DARKIRONDWARF_FEMALE = "Known for their fiery temperament and unshakeable resolve, the Dark Iron dwarves have long been at odds with the other clans: a failed coup in Ironforge sparked the War of the Three Hammers, and many Dark Irons fought in the name of Ragnaros, the Firelord. Although part of the clan has sworn allegiance to Regent Queen Moira Thaurissan, the rest refuse to rejoin their kin. Yet the Alliance needs a united Dark Iron clan to harness the power of Azerite in its war against the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_ZANDALARITROLL = "The Zandalari are a proud people whose origins reach back to the earliest days of Azeroth's history. Their fierce warriors ride dinosaurs into battle, and their fleet ranks among the most formidable in the known world. Alas, between enemy incursions and turmoil within the royal council, the kingdom's foundations are under threat. Should the heroes of the Horde manage to restore balance to Zandalar, they will gain a powerful ally.";
RACE_INFO_ZANDALARITROLL_FEMALE = "The Zandalari are a proud people whose origins reach back to the earliest days of Azeroth's history. Their fierce warriors ride dinosaurs into battle, and their fleet ranks among the most formidable in the known world. Alas, between enemy incursions and turmoil within the royal council, the kingdom's foundations are under threat. Should the heroes of the Horde manage to restore balance to Zandalar, they will gain a powerful ally.";
RACE_INFO_LIGHTFORGED = "For millennia, the Army of the Light has waged war against the Burning Legion in the twisted Void. The draenei most devoted to this endless crusade underwent the Lightforging ritual, binding their physical forms to the very essence of the holy Light. Finally victorious on Argus, the Lightforged draenei have set themselves a new mission: to protect Azeroth from every threat and help the Alliance repel the Horde's assaults.";
RACE_INFO_LIGHTFORGED_FEMALE = "For millennia, the Army of the Light has waged war against the Burning Legion in the twisted Void. The draenei most devoted to this endless crusade underwent the Lightforging ritual, binding their physical forms to the very essence of the holy Light. Finally victorious on Argus, the Lightforged draenei have set themselves a new mission: to protect Azeroth from every threat and help the Alliance repel the Horde's assaults.";
RACE_INFO_NIGHTELF_DH = "Ten thousand years ago, the night elves founded a vast empire, but their reckless use of magic led to their downfall. Wracked with grief, they withdrew into the forests and remained isolated until the return of their ancient enemy, the Burning Legion. Left with no alternative, the night elves emerged from their isolation to defend their place in the new world.";
RACE_INFO_NIGHTELF_DH_FEMALE = "Ten thousand years ago, the night elves founded a vast empire, but their reckless use of magic led to their downfall. Wracked with grief, they withdrew into the forests and remained isolated until the return of their ancient enemy, the Burning Legion. Left with no alternative, the night elves emerged from their isolation to defend their place in the new world.";
RACE_INFO_BLOODELF_DH = "Exiled high elves once founded Quel'Thalas, where they created a magical fountain called the Sunwell. They benefited from its power but gradually grew dependent on it.|n|nMany centuries later, the undead Scourge destroyed the Sunwell and killed most of the high elves. The scattered survivors, now known as blood elves, are rebuilding Quel'Thalas and seeking new sources of magic to soothe their painful cravings.";
RACE_INFO_BLOODELF_DH_FEMALE = "Exiled high elves once founded Quel'Thalas, where they created a magical fountain called the Sunwell. They benefited from its power but gradually grew dependent on it.|n|nMany centuries later, the undead Scourge destroyed the Sunwell and killed most of the high elves. The scattered survivors, now known as blood elves, are rebuilding Quel'Thalas and seeking new sources of magic to soothe their painful cravings.";
RACE_INFO_PANDAREN_H = "Wrapped in mystery and legend, the pandaren long remained an enigma to the other races of Azeroth. Those who follow the Way of the Tushui believe there is an absolute morality in this world: a single path of good and evil. As this philosophy aligns closely with the ideals of the Alliance, it was only natural for the Tushui to pledge their allegiance to it.";
RACE_INFO_PANDAREN_H_FEMALE = "Wrapped in mystery and legend, the pandaren long remained an enigma to the other races of Azeroth. Those who follow the Way of the Tushui believe there is an absolute morality in this world: a single path of good and evil. As this philosophy aligns closely with the ideals of the Alliance, it was only natural for the Tushui to pledge their allegiance to it.";
RACE_INFO_PANDAREN_A = "Wrapped in mystery and legend, the pandaren long remained an enigma to the other races of Azeroth. Those who follow the Way of the Tushui believe there is an absolute morality in this world: a single path of good and evil. As this philosophy aligns closely with the ideals of the Alliance, it was only natural for the Tushui to pledge their allegiance to it.";
RACE_INFO_PANDAREN_A_FEMALE = "Wrapped in mystery and legend, the pandaren long remained an enigma to the other races of Azeroth. Those who follow the Way of the Tushui believe there is an absolute morality in this world: a single path of good and evil. As this philosophy aligns closely with the ideals of the Alliance, it was only natural for the Tushui to pledge their allegiance to it.";
RACE_INFO_VULPERA = "Resourceful and clever, the vulpera have survived in the harsh desert of Vol'dun for generations. Organized into tightly knit caravans, they watch out for one another as they cross the dunes in search of supplies to scavenge. Despite their small size, vulpera are fierce and cunning in battle, and any enemy careless enough to underestimate them quickly regrets it. Now full members of the Horde, they have left the sands behind with their wagons to set out on a new adventure.";
RACE_INFO_VULPERA_FEMALE = "Resourceful and clever, the vulpera have survived in the harsh desert of Vol'dun for generations. Organized into tightly knit caravans, they watch out for one another as they cross the dunes in search of supplies to scavenge. Despite their small size, vulpera are fierce and cunning in battle, and any enemy careless enough to underestimate them quickly regrets it. Now full members of the Horde, they have left the sands behind with their wagons to set out on a new adventure.";
RACE_INFO_EREDAR = "The Man'ari Eredar are corrupted Eredar demons who currently lead the Burning Legion. After witnessing the corruption and the many catastrophic decisions made by Sargeras, his right hand Kil'Vajash decided to rebel against the Burning Legion. Overwhelmed by Sargeras's endless armies, he opened a portal and led his followers to a lost fragment of Marduum to seek refuge.";
RACE_INFO_EREDAR_FEMALE = "The Man'ari Eredar are corrupted Eredar demons who currently lead the Burning Legion. After witnessing the corruption and the many catastrophic decisions made by Sargeras, his right hand Kil'Vajash decided to rebel against the Burning Legion. Overwhelmed by Sargeras's endless armies, he opened a portal and led his followers to a lost fragment of Marduum to seek refuge.";
RACE_INFO_VOIDELF = "Many have tried to master the corrupting magic of the Void, and most have descended into madness. Determined to use these powers for the good of Azeroth, Alleria Windrunner is the first mortal to resist the whispers of the shadows. She has since rushed to the aid of a group of her kin on the verge of succumbing to darkness, and has sworn to train these Void Elves to control their share of Shadow. Together, they will put their new powers to the service of the Alliance.";
RACE_INFO_VOIDELF_FEMALE = "Many have tried to master the corrupting magic of the Void, and most have descended into madness. Determined to use these powers for the good of Azeroth, Alleria Windrunner is the first mortal to resist the whispers of the shadows. She has since rushed to the aid of a group of her kin on the verge of succumbing to darkness, and has sworn to train these Void Elves to control their share of Shadow. Together, they will put their new powers to the service of the Alliance.";
RACE_INFO_NIGHTBORNE = "The Nightborne of Suramar spent millennia isolated behind an arcane barrier, slowly transformed by the magic of the Nightwell. These proud, noble elves now seek to reclaim their place in Azeroth.";
RACE_INFO_NIGHTBORNE_FEMALE = "The Nightborne of Suramar spent millennia isolated behind an arcane barrier, slowly transformed by the magic of the Nightwell. These proud, noble elves now seek to reclaim their place in Azeroth.";
RACE_INFO_BLOODELF = "Long ago the exiled high elves founded Quel'Thalas, where they created a magical fount called the Sunwell. Though they were strengthened by its powers, they also grew increasingly dependent on them.|n|nAges later the undead Scourge destroyed the Sunwell and most of the high elf population. Now called blood elves, these scattered refugees are rebuilding Quel'Thalas as they search for a new magic source to satisfy their painful addiction.";
RACE_INFO_BLOODELF_FEMALE = "Long ago the exiled high elves founded Quel'Thalas, where they created a magical fount called the Sunwell. Though they were strengthened by its powers, they also grew increasingly dependent on them.|n|nAges later the undead Scourge destroyed the Sunwell and most of the high elf population. Now called blood elves, these scattered refugees are rebuilding Quel'Thalas as they search for a new magic source to satisfy their painful addiction.";
RACE_INFO_DRAENEI = "Driven from their home world of Argus, the honorable draenei fled the Burning Legion for eons before finding a remote planet to settle on. They shared this world with the shamanistic orcs and named it Draenor. In time the Legion corrupted the orcs, who waged war and nearly exterminated the peaceful draenei. A lucky few fled to Azeroth, where they now seek allies in their battle against the Burning Legion.";
RACE_INFO_DRAENEI_FEMALE = "Driven from their home world of Argus, the honorable draenei fled the Burning Legion for eons before finding a remote planet to settle on. They shared this world with the shamanistic orcs and named it Draenor. In time the Legion corrupted the orcs, who waged war and nearly exterminated the peaceful draenei. A lucky few fled to Azeroth, where they now seek allies in their battle against the Burning Legion.";
RACE_INFO_DWARF = "In ages past, the dwarves cared only for riches taken from the earth's depths. Then records surfaced of a god-like race said to have given the dwarves life... and an enchanted birthright. Driven to learn more, the dwarves devoted themselves to the pursuit of lost artifacts and ancient knowledge. Today dwarven archaeologists are scattered throughout the globe.";
RACE_INFO_DWARF_FEMALE = "In ages past, the dwarves cared only for riches taken from the earth's depths. Then records surfaced of a god-like race said to have given the dwarves life... and an enchanted birthright. Driven to learn more, the dwarves devoted themselves to the pursuit of lost artifacts and ancient knowledge. Today dwarven archaeologists are scattered throughout the globe.";
RACE_INFO_GNOME = "Though small in stature, the gnomes of Khaz Modan have used their great intellect to secure a place in history. Indeed, their subterranean kingdom, Gnomeregan, was once a marvel of steam-driven technology. Even so, due to a massive trogg invasion, the city was lost. Now its builders are vagabonds in the dwarven lands, aiding their allies as best they can.";
RACE_INFO_GNOME_FEMALE = "Though small in stature, the gnomes of Khaz Modan have used their great intellect to secure a place in history. Indeed, their subterranean kingdom, Gnomeregan, was once a marvel of steam-driven technology. Even so, due to a massive trogg invasion, the city was lost. Now its builders are vagabonds in the dwarven lands, aiding their allies as best they can.";
RACE_INFO_HUMAN = "Humans are a young race, and thus highly versatile, mastering the arts of combat, craftsmanship, and magic with stunning efficiency. The humans’ valor and optimism have led them to build some of the world’s greatest kingdoms. In this troubled era, after generations of conflict, humanity seeks to rekindle its former glory and forge a shining new future.";
RACE_INFO_HUMAN_FEMALE = "Humans are a young race, and thus highly versatile, mastering the arts of combat, craftsmanship, and magic with stunning efficiency. The humans’ valor and optimism have led them to build some of the world’s greatest kingdoms. In this troubled era, after generations of conflict, humanity seeks to rekindle its former glory and forge a shining new future.";
RACE_INFO_NIGHTELF = "Ten thousand years ago, the night elves founded a vast empire, but their reckless use of primal magic brought them to ruin. In grief, they withdrew to the forests and remained isolated there until the return of their ancient enemy, the Burning Legion. With no other choice, the night elves emerged at last from their seclusion to fight for their place in the new world.";
RACE_INFO_NIGHTELF_FEMALE = "Ten thousand years ago, the night elves founded a vast empire, but their reckless use of primal magic brought them to ruin. In grief, they withdrew to the forests and remained isolated there until the return of their ancient enemy, the Burning Legion. With no other choice, the night elves emerged at last from their seclusion to fight for their place in the new world.";
RACE_INFO_ORC = "The orc race originated on the planet Draenor. A peaceful people with shamanic beliefs, they were enslaved by the Burning Legion and forced into war with the humans of Azeroth. Although it took many years, the orcs finally escaped the demons' corruption and won their freedom. To this day they fight for honor in an alien world that hates and reviles them.";
RACE_INFO_ORC_FEMALE = "The orc race originated on the planet Draenor. A peaceful people with shamanic beliefs, they were enslaved by the Burning Legion and forced into war with the humans of Azeroth. Although it took many years, the orcs finally escaped the demons' corruption and won their freedom. To this day they fight for honor in an alien world that hates and reviles them.";
RACE_INFO_SCOURGE = "Free of the Lich King's grasp, the Forsaken seek to overthrow his rule. Led by the banshee Sylvanas, they hunger for vengeance against the Scourge. Humans, too, have become the enemy, relentless in their drive to purge all undead from the land. The Forsaken care little even for their allies; to them the Horde is merely a tool that may further their dark schemes.";
RACE_INFO_SCOURGE_FEMALE = "Free of the Lich King's grasp, the Forsaken seek to overthrow his rule. Led by the banshee Sylvanas, they hunger for vengeance against the Scourge. Humans, too, have become the enemy, relentless in their drive to purge all undead from the land. The Forsaken care little even for their allies; to them the Horde is merely a tool that may further their dark schemes.";
RACE_INFO_TAUREN = "Always the tauren strive to preserve the balance of nature and heed the will of their goddess, the Earth Mother. Recently attacked by murderous centaur, the tauren would have been wiped out, save for a chance encounter with the orcs, who helped defeat the interlopers. To honor this blood-debt, the tauren joined the Horde, solidifying the two races' friendship.";
RACE_INFO_TAUREN_FEMALE = "Always the tauren strive to preserve the balance of nature and heed the will of their goddess, the Earth Mother. Recently attacked by murderous centaur, the tauren would have been wiped out, save for a chance encounter with the orcs, who helped defeat the interlopers. To honor this blood-debt, the tauren joined the Horde, solidifying the two races' friendship.";
RACE_INFO_TROLL = "Once at home in the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, the fierce trolls of the Darkspear tribe were pushed out by warring factions. Eventually the trolls befriended the orcish Horde, and Thrall, the orcs' young warchief, convinced the trolls to travel with him to Kalimdor. Though they cling to their shadowy heritage, the Darkspear trolls hold a place of honor in the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_TROLL_FEMALE = "Once at home in the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, the fierce trolls of the Darkspear tribe were pushed out by warring factions. Eventually the trolls befriended the orcish Horde, and Thrall, the orcs' young warchief, convinced the trolls to travel with him to Kalimdor. Though they cling to their shadowy heritage, the Darkspear trolls hold a place of honor in the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_GOBLIN_ = "Once inhabitants of the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, the fierce Darkspear trolls were driven out by warring factions. The trolls eventually befriended the orc Horde, and Thrall, the young orc chieftain, convinced them to journey with him to Kalimdor. Though they refuse to abandon their dark heritage, the Darkspear trolls hold a place of honor within the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_GOBLIN__FEMALE = "Once inhabitants of the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, the fierce Darkspear trolls were driven out by warring factions. The trolls eventually befriended the orc Horde, and Thrall, the young orc chieftain, convinced them to journey with him to Kalimdor. Though they refuse to abandon their dark heritage, the Darkspear trolls hold a place of honor within the Horde.";
RACE_INFO_WORGEN = "Humans are a young race of remarkably varied talents, mastering the arts of combat, craftsmanship, and magic with astonishing efficiency. Human valor and optimism have led them to build some of the greatest kingdoms in the world. In this troubled age, after generations of conflict, humanity longs to rekindle its past glory and forge a bright new future.";
RACE_INFO_WORGEN_FEMALE = "Humans are a young race of remarkably varied talents, mastering the arts of combat, craftsmanship, and magic with astonishing efficiency. Human valor and optimism have led them to build some of the greatest kingdoms in the world. In this troubled age, after generations of conflict, humanity longs to rekindle its past glory and forge a bright new future.";
